# NO /category/* or /collection/* splat.
#
# These two rules used to rewrite every category and collection URL to a single
# client-rendered document. _redirects is consulted BEFORE a matching static
# asset is served (the reverse of what the note at the top of this file assumed
# and what the Cloudflare docs imply), so the splat also shadowed real files:
# with /category/fiction/index.html on disk, /category/fiction/ still returned
# the generic client-rendered page. Every /category/<slug>/ and
# /collection/<slug>/ is a generated page now, so nothing needs the rewrite —
# and with it gone an unbuilt slug correctly 404s instead of answering 200 with
# an empty duplicate. generate_site.py writes a page for EVERY category any
# link names, so no internal link relies on the fallback.
#
# /category/?name=<X> and /collection/?id=<X> still work: their path is
# /category/ and /collection/, which are real files.


# No catch-all: Pages serves the generated 404.html for anything unmatched.
# That keeps admin-created product pages (whose Lambda is not ported yet) out
# of the index as real 404s instead of soft-200 duplicate homepages.
